      diveDeep: 'Key organelle comparison: Plant cells have (that animal cells lack): chloroplasts, large central vacuole, cell wall (cellulose). Animal cells have (that plant cells lack): centrioles, lysosomes (more prominent). Both have: cell membrane, nucleus, mitochondria, ribosomes, ER, Golgi. Mitochondria (choice A) are in BOTH plant and animal cells — plants need ATP for cellular respiration too. The nucleus (choice B) is in both types. Ribosomes (choice D) are in all cells — even prokaryotes. Plant cells also have a cell wall (made of cellulose) and a large central vacuole for water storage and turgor pressure. Students should memorize this comparison table for the Regents.',
